/name incident-response
/description Security incident response with parallel investigation and human approval
/trigger manual
/budget 20.00
/timeout 1800000

# Phase 1: Parallel investigation by specialist agents
/parallel
  /spawn log-analyst "Search all log files for the incident timeframe. Extract: affected services, timestamps, user IDs, IP addresses. Report every finding with file:line."
  /spawn code-investigator "Search codebase for recent changes related to the affected services. Look for: commits around the incident time, auth changes, config changes, dependency updates. Report file:line for every finding."
  /spawn dependency-scanner "Check all dependencies for known vulnerabilities matching the incident characteristics. Report package name, version, CVE, and remediation."
/end

# Phase 2: Wait for all investigators
/join log-analyst code-investigator dependency-scanner

# Phase 3: Synthesize findings
/spawn incident-commander
/seed incident-commander assistant "I've dispatched 3 investigation teams. Gathering their reports now."
/collect log-analyst code-investigator dependency-scanner -> incident-commander
/msg incident-commander "All investigation reports are above. Synthesize a timeline of events, identify the root cause, assess impact (data/customers/systems), and recommend immediate remediation steps. Be specific — cite file:line for every claim."
/wait incident-commander complete

# Phase 4: Human decides response
/approve "Investigation complete. Escalate to security team?"

/log "Incident response complete"
